This is not such a great idea.  Whenever the little bastards swipe
something from me, it is usually something like teleport control,
poison/fire/cold resistance or speed (this last is a real pain in the
butt).  Messing with gremlins is playing with fire.  I'd just say that
the easiest way to deal with intrinsic invisibility and shopkeepers is
to just wait until you get teleport control and teleport into the shop
and buy whatever you like.  Make sure you have a way to teleport out,
though.  This has the added side benefit of being an easy way to cream
the shopkeeper (NOTE:  this may no longer be true in 3.1.x.  It was in
3.0j, and I haven't tried it in 3.1.x).  In 3.0j, if you were invisible
in a shop, the shopkeeper would stand still at the door.  So, just stand
back and zap wands, cast spells and throw stuff until the shopkeeper
snuffs it.

